---
import SubLayout from "../layouts/SubLayout.astro";
import Card from "../components/Card.astro";
import AboutMeIcon from "../components/svgs/AboutMeIcon.astro";
import MeCard from "../components/MeCard.astro";
---

<SubLayout title="Dylan - About Me">
    <Card
        href="javascript:history.back()"
        title="About Me"
        body="Learn about me and my journey to becoming a programmer. I have learned a lot over the years and I am still learning. I am always looking for new things to learn."
        nolineclamp
        cursor
        onlypopout
    >
        <AboutMeIcon />
    </Card>
    <MeCard name="My Journey">
        I started wanting to be a programmer when I was around 9 years old.
        I got interested in the complex games I played and wanted to know how they worked.
        At first, I didn't think I had the skills to become a programmer, but I decided to start learning.
        <br /><br />
        I took in-person classes to learn how to make games in Scratch, and that really helped me understand programming and how it functions.
        I then started to learn HTML, CSS, and Javascript. This allowed me much more freedom than Scratch, and I was able to express my creativity with much more complex projects.
    </MeCard>
</SubLayout>
